     "head": "शि��ुर्वेेशि� प�ुर्वेेशि� र्वेेशि� गाान रसंं फशि�: Shishurvetti pashurvetti, vetti gaana rasam phanihi A child, an animal, a snake, all can respond to and appreciate music Have you noticed what people do when they listen to music? Sometimes we tap our feet, or we nod to the rhythm. Sometimes we may sway as per the melody, or move our fingers. These are all ways that we naturally respond to music. Discuss:  When do you like to listen to music?  What is your favourite song or piece of music?  How do you feel when you hear it? ACTIVITY 14.1 Responding to Music  Find a place to stand comfortably in the class. With all the students spread out close your eyes.  Your teacher will play a piece of music.  Listen to it intently and let your body naturally respond to it. Do you want to move your arms? Or sway your head? Do you feel like moving your fingers, or twirling around? Remember, no on"
    },
